# >>> baseline: secrets and sensitive data never go in git
# Managed by baseline-update (it rewrites this block). Put the project's own rules outside it; to allow one
# harmless file that matches (a public test certificate, an example), add "!path/to/file" below the block.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.ppk
*.kdbx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.netrc
secrets/
.secrets/
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.json
credentials.json
token.json
service-account*.json
*.secret
# <<< baseline: secrets
